// expect: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// An explicit read whose bounds nothing on its path proves keeps the
// primitive's check, so its row carries the Trap and `!Trap` is refused.
// The claim holds through the one call, so `mentl check` names no pending
// claim here, but the row is not read through the calls and keeps the Trap.
fn pick(xs, i) with !Trap = list_index(xs, i)

fn main() = pick([1, 2, 3], 1)
